call sites in the eight resource classes now go through
$self->_normalise_filters($opts{filters}).

Rules, each one a measured daemon response (Podman 5.4.2 / API 1.41, GET
/v1.41/images/json, 2026-08-27):
  - bare value wrapped into an ArrayRef  ({"dangling":"true"} was 500)
  - elements stringified                 ({"dangling":[1]}   was 500)
  - JSON->true/false and \1/\0 -> "true"/"false" ({"dangling":true} / [true] were 500)
  - undef, empty string, any other ref, empty filter name -> croak
  - empty ArrayRef passes through (measured 200, filters nothing)

The boolean rewrite is bound to the value's TYPE, not to its truthiness and
not to the filter name: a plain 1 becomes "1", so exited => [0], stars => [0]
and label => [1] keep asking what they asked. JSON->true / \1 carry the claim
of being booleans and are also the two forms encode_json would otherwise turn
into a JSON true, which the daemon rejects.

Correction to this ticket's premise: a wrong SHAPE is not silent on Podman --
it is a 500 carrying a Go unmarshal message, one round trip later, naming
neither the option nor the key. What the fix changes is where that is said,
and for the recoverable shapes it repairs instead of refusing.

